(6810556, 1022932, 136235, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by NiallOTuama:</b></div><hr/><i> Thanks for writing in the comments. Geez, that seems excessive for a soccer game? When Ireland lost we cheered... though we had no expectations really. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Yeah people were pretty extreme, though in the end I think most of those rioting were already decided on starting a riot (or setting off their fireworks at least) and losing the match was more of a trigger.<br/> <br/>ETA: then again.. if France had won there probably would have been more celebratory fireworks and flares than bottles.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2012-07-06 07:41:53.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by NiallOTuama: Thanks for writing in the comments. Geez, that seems excessive for a soccer game? When Ireland lost we cheered... though we had no expectations really.   Yeah people were pretty extreme, though in the end I think most of those rioting were already decided on starting a riot (or setting off their fireworks at least) and losing the match was more of a trigger. ETA: then again.. if France had won there probably would have been more celebratory fireworks and flares than bottles.', '2012-07-06 08:40:39.000000', '2012-07-06 08:41:53.000000', 0),
